      "writtenOn": "2017-07-28T00:04:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It can be added to any power state driver if needed. Look at it this way -- I could have replaced the \"#ifdef S3_USB_WAKE\" in all of the code here with \"#if CONFIG_CHIPSET_POWER_SEQ_VERSION \u003e\u003d 2\". But adding a new #define is better, because:\n\n1) It\u0027s easier to understand what the #ifdef\u0027d code does.\n2) I don\u0027t know for sure that this feature will stick around for future board versions.\n\nOther power state drivers that implement this feature don\u0027t need a define at all. We only need it here because we have several different power signal configs, and we\u0027re trying to reuse code.",
